# Build context exclusions for the API image.
#
# The build context for this image is the backend directory. Everything listed
# here is either a secret, a build artifact, or code that has no business
# running in production. Two of the entries below are load bearing rather than
# tidy-minded:
#
#   .env  A local environment file copied into an image is a credential baked
#         into a layer, readable by anyone who can pull the image. The
#         Dockerfile never copies it, and this makes that a guarantee rather
#         than an assumption about a future edit.
#
#   tests, alembic
#         Kept out so the image carries only what serves requests. Migrations
#         are applied by the pipeline before the revision is deployed, so
#         shipping them would add weight and imply a start-up path that does
#         not exist.

# Secrets. Nothing in this group may ever enter a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
gcp-credentials*.json

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python bytecode and virtual environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches. These are large, machine specific and useless in an image.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Tests and their fixtures. Not served, not shipped. The dev dependency group
# in pyproject.toml is not installed by the image either, so nothing here has
# anything to run against.
tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini

# Migrations. Applied by the pipeline, never from container start-up.
alembic/
alembic.ini

# Development utilities. Seeding is run from a developer machine or from the
# pipeline, against a database, and has no business inside the serving image.
seed.py

# Container files, which would only invalidate cache layers
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# Documentation, with one exception. README.md must stay in the context because
# pyproject.toml names it in its "readme" field, and the install fails with a
# confusing packaging error if it is absent.
*.md
!README.md
